---
// The glass both hero devices are made of: one pane, frosted, lighter toward the top, with a thin
// rim of light brightest along the top and fading down the sides. It fills its parent; the shape
// around it sets three values, so a phone and a window are the same material at different sizes:
//   --pane-radius  the corner (the smoothing is added here)
//   --pane-frost   how far the blur reaches
//   --pane-rim     the rim's width
// and two strengths, for a darker photograph behind it:
//   --pane-light   the light at the top of the pane (0.16)
//   --pane-edge    how bright the rim stays down the sides (0.22, at half height)
// It fades from inside, by --presence (global.css): to bring it in, animate that on a container,
// never opacity, which would stop it frosting until the fade ends. The shape's other layers take
// --presence too.
---

<div class="pane"></div>

<style>
  .pane,
  .pane::before {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: calc(var(--pane-radius) * var(--corner-reach));
    corner-shape: var(--corner);
  }

  .pane {
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      rgba(255, 255, 255, var(--pane-light, 0.16)),
      rgba(255, 255, 255, calc(var(--pane-light, 0.16) * 0.45)) 24%,
      rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04) 60%
    );
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--pane-frost)) saturate(1.1);
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--pane-frost)) saturate(1.1);
    /* Just enough shade outside the rim to lift the pane off a bright sky. */
    box-shadow: 0 calc(var(--pane-frost) * 0.4) calc(var(--pane-frost) * 2.5) rgba(30, 24, 44, 0.12);
    opacity: var(--presence);
  }

  /* The rim is a masked ring of its own, light only, because an element that frosts cannot also be
     masked with smoothed corners in Chromium. */
  .pane::before {
    content: '';
    border: var(--pane-rim) solid transparent;
    background: linear-gradient(
        180deg,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95),
        rgba(255, 255, 255, calc(0.38 + var(--pane-edge, 0.22))) 18%,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, var(--pane-edge, 0.22)) 50%,
        rgba(255, 255, 255, calc(var(--pane-edge, 0.22) * 0.27)) 80%
      )
      border-box;
    -webkit-mask:
      linear-gradient(#000 0 0) padding-box exclude,
      linear-gradient(#000 0 0) border-box;
    mask:
      linear-gradient(#000 0 0) padding-box exclude,
      linear-gradient(#000 0 0) border-box;
  }
</style>
